From: Prabhsimran Singh <prabhsimrans@nvidia.com>
Subject: ggml-cuda: re-instantiate CUDA graphs that sat idle on integrated GPUs

On Jetson Thor (L4T R38.3, driver 580), a cached executable can fault
(Xid 13) or give wrong results after the GPU power-gates while idle. A new
instance of the same graph is correct.

A pause longer than GGML_CUDA_GRAPH_REINSTANTIATE_AFTER_MS on a device
starts a new idle epoch. Executables from an earlier epoch are instantiated
again before they run. Default: 250 ms on integrated GPUs, off on discrete
GPUs. If the instantiation fails, the call runs the graph nodes directly.

Upstream: stays here as a workaround until the Thor driver is fixed.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/common.cuh b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/common.cuh
index b7bcc820beb85dcb695398eaa2eac0e94469871b..47aee26bbbb6b87ae0f357a64455bed3e4fa6e75 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/common.cuh
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/common.cuh
@@ -1295,6 +1295,7 @@ struct ggml_cuda_graph {
     bool warmup_complete = false;
     uint64_t uid = 0;
     int64_t last_used_time = 0;
+    uint64_t idle_epoch = 0; // ggml_cuda_idle_epoch() at the last launch
     struct node_properties {
         ggml_tensor node;
